            ("What is the nearest major spiral galaxy to the Milky Way, destined to collide and merge with our galaxy in about 4.5 billion years?", "The Andromeda Galaxy (Messier 31 / M31)", ["The Triangulum Galaxy (M33)", "The Large Magellanic Cloud", "The Small Magellanic Cloud"], "Andromeda is a spiral galaxy situated approximately 2.5 million light-years from Earth, approaching at 110 km/second."),
            ("What astronomical unit of length is defined as the average distance between the center of the Earth and the center of the Sun (about 93 million miles)?", "Astronomical Unit (AU)", ["Light-Year", "Parsec", "Kiloparsec"], "One AU equals exactly 149,597,870,700 meters, serving as the standard distance scale within our Solar System."),
            ("What astronomical distance unit defines the physical distance that a light photon travels through a vacuum in one Julian year (about 5.88 trillion miles)?", "Light-Year (ly)", ["Astronomical Unit (AU)", "Parsec (pc)", "Megaparsec"], "A light-year measures distance rather than time, equaling approximately 9.46 trillion kilometers (5.88 trillion miles)."),
            ("What astronomical distance unit, equal to approximately 3.26 light-years, is based on the parallax angle of one arcsecond across Earth\'s orbit?", "Parsec (pc)", ["Light-Year", "Astronomical Unit", "Fermi"], "Parallax-second ('parsec') is the preferred unit among astrophysicists for measuring distances to stars and distant galaxies."),
            ("What is the closest star system to our Solar System, located approximately 4.24 light-years away from Earth?", "Alpha Centauri (specifically Proxima Centauri)", ["Barnard\'s Star", "Sirius (Dog Star)", "Wolf 359"], "Proxima Centauri is a faint red dwarf star in the triple-star Alpha Centauri system, orbited by terrestrial exoplanets."),
            ("What is the brightest individual star visible in the night sky as seen from Earth, located in the constellation Canis Major?", "Sirius (The Dog Star)", ["Betelgeuse", "Rigel", "Vega"], "Sirius has an apparent visual magnitude of -1.46, shining brightly due to its luminosity and proximity (8.6 light-years)."),
            ("What thermonuclear process in the core of our Sun converts hydrogen nuclei into helium, releasing colossal radiant energy?", "Nuclear Fusion (Proton-Proton Chain)", ["Nuclear Fission", "Radioactive Alpha Decay", "Chemical Combustion"], "Every second, the Sun fuses 600 million tons of hydrogen into helium, converting mass deficit directly into solar radiation."),
            ("What visible surface layer of the Sun emits the sunlight and light photons that we observe from Earth?", "The Photosphere", ["The Chromosphere", "The Corona", "The Radiation Zone"], "The photosphere is a 300-mile-thick plasma layer with an effective surface temperature of approximately 5,500 degrees Celsius (9,900 F)."),
            ("What tenuous, high-temperature outermost plasma atmosphere of the Sun is visible to the naked eye as a white halo only during a total solar eclipse?", "The Corona", ["The Photosphere", "The Chromosphere", "The Convective Zone"], "The solar corona reaches temperatures exceeding 1 to 3 million Kelvin, accelerated by magnetic reconnection events."),
            ("What stream of charged plasma particles (electrons and protons) ejected from the Sun\'s corona flows continuously through the Solar System?", "The Solar Wind", ["Cosmic Rays", "The Van Allen Belt", "Coronal Mass Discharge"], "The solar wind travels at 400 to 800 km/s, carving the heliosphere bubble and driving auroras on magnetized planets."),
            ("What temporary dark blemishes on the Sun\'s photosphere are caused by intense localized magnetic field flux inhibiting convection?", "Sunspots", ["Solar Flares", "Coronal Holes", "Prominences"], "Sunspots appear darker because their intense magnetic fields cool them to ~3,800 K compared to surrounding 5,800 K plasma."),
